autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "s", "argument_id": "a4a5f0ee-7388-4e62-a55b-9d8629af3d0f", "id": "46aab076-b98d-4da5-852f-3f85018de21e", "reason": "The Tid\u00f6 bloc's 173 mandates fall below the 175 threshold required to block an S-led prime minister, so even a fully united bloc cannot prevent an S-led government; moreover the bloc is internally divided (KD open to a cross-bloc reserve, L negotiating broadly, SD's demands straining cohesion), so M cannot credibly claim to lead a united alternative. The claimed V-C contradiction is also not binding: V has accepted a support-partner role without government participation and C has confirmed V's strong formal influence, so the S+C+MP+V package remains coherent and verifiable."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "mp", "argument_id": "a4a5f0ee-7388-4e62-a55b-9d8629af3d0f", "id": "6407cc71-c1f6-4abd-b1b1-aa04202fab97", "reason": "SD's claim to lead a credible, united Tid\u00f6 alternative is not verifiable: the bloc's internal divisions are already surfacing (KD's openness to a cross-bloc reserve and L-SD tensions on economics), and at 173 mandates it is short of the 175 no-vote threshold, so it cannot block an S-led government on its own. Meanwhile the S+C+MP+V construction is actively progressing and binding: S has booked the joint concretization round and offered V an institutionalized, non-circumventable budget/reform role with independent follow-up, so the left package is being made concrete and verifiable rather than remaining the 'contradictory, non-binding' construct SD portrays. SD's effect therefore rests on a fragile bloc and a mischaracterized rival path, limiting its credibility and durability."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "v", "argument_id": "a4a5f0ee-7388-4e62-a55b-9d8629af3d0f", "id": "68be0168-be2d-4412-a904-3e5f9ce819f8", "reason": "SD's desired effect rests on two false premises. First, the Tid\u00f6 bloc is not a coherent, united 173: KD has opened for a cross-bloc reserve toward S and L-SD economic tensions are straining cohesion (effect 55a733d5), so the '173 mandates intact' claim is fragmented and does not constitute a credible alternative. Second, the alleged V-C contradiction is not fatal: V has accepted a formally established support-partner (tolerance/abstention) role, not government participation, so it does not conflict with C's red line; the S+C+MP+V package can be made binding and verifiable through an institutionalized, non-bypassable budget/reform role and an independent annual review mechanism that S, C, and MP have all accepted as the basis. SD therefore cannot credibly undermine the S-led package or hold the bloc together."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "c", "argument_id": "a4a5f0ee-7388-4e62-a55b-9d8629af3d0f", "id": "be0e1a00-6ed8-4a21-9cd5-5bf5fc87bd2a", "reason": "SD's claim that the S+C+MP+V package is 'internally contradictory' and 'not binding or verifiable' fails: C has already accepted a formal cooperation agreement giving V strong, visible, binding influence (real budget negotiation, a joint reform council with clear mandate, and measurable commitments with independent follow-up) with V outside government, which resolves the alleged V-C contradiction and makes V's tolerance verifiable and locked. Moreover, the Tid\u00f6 bloc cannot actually govern without C's abstention/support, which C has explicitly declined, so its 'credible alternative leader' claim is hollow; and internal tensions (KD's openness to a center reserve, L-SD economic friction, and M's own exploration of an M+KD+L path without SD in government) fragment the 173-mandate bloc's cohesion rather than uniting it."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "kd", "argument_id": "a4a5f0ee-7388-4e62-a55b-9d8629af3d0f", "id": "f88068c0-c0a1-4330-9fb1-4ec871233187", "reason": "SD's 'united opposition' framing is not a credible viable alternative: no Tid\u00f6 configuration can pass the 175-test because C's red line against SD in government and SD's own insistence on participation are both firm, so the bloc's 173 mandates cannot form a government. A 'united opposition' that cannot govern is hollow as an alternative, and locking KD into it forfeits KD's v\u00e5gm\u00e4stare leverage to secure influence in a functioning government - so the desired effect of a credible bloc preventing KD defection fails."}
