autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "sd", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "10c0c0d5-1b2c-41ef-a7d3-309cdd77755a", "reason": "KD's mitten S+C+MP+KD (169) is not robust or viable: it needs 6 non-NO votes from the 180 outside seats, but V will not abstain for a package that keeps V out of government (V demands formal participation or decisive influence and has itself signalled the package is too symbolic to justify abstention), and L is a Tid\u00f6 party that would vote NO against an S-led government. Moreover, per regeringsregler \u00a76.1 KD cannot unilaterally bind S, C, and MP to include KD in government, and C has publicly committed to S+C+MP with V as tolerating support party \u2014 so the mitten is not an agreed or verifiable configuration and cannot credibly pass the 175-test."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "m", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "2e65a6c6-6cae-4970-af33-d097ef78a565", "reason": "KD's robust mitten S+C+MP+KD cannot form or pass: MP has publicly and repeatedly refused to sit in any government that includes KD (or L, M, SD), so the configuration lacks a necessary government partner from the outset. Even setting that aside, the mitten passes the 175-test only if V or L abstains, but V will not tolerate a Tid\u00f6/right party (KD) in government and would vote NO, while L (a Tid\u00f6 party) will not enable a government that excludes M and seats KD with the left \u2014 if both vote NO, NO=M+SD+L+V=180>175 and it collapses. KD cannot credibly claim Tid\u00f6 as first-hand while simultaneously advancing a mitten that breaks Tid\u00f6, so the package lacks internal coherence and credibility."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "s", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "3a5ed2f7-0196-4fd8-81a9-6a799e3cb4ff", "reason": "KD:s S+C+MP+KD (169) kan inte trov\u00e4rdigt klara 175-testet: MP har en uttalad r\u00f6d linje mot KD i regeringen och skulle inte ing\u00e5 i en s\u00e5dan regering, och 169-konfigurationen kr\u00e4ver \u00e4nd\u00e5 V:s (eller L:s) nedlagda r\u00f6st f\u00f6r att n\u00e5 175 \u2014 men V har uttryckligen v\u00e4grat l\u00e4gga ner r\u00f6sten f\u00f6r ett paket som utesluter V fr\u00e5n reellt inflytande. D\u00e4rmed \u00e4r 'den robusta mitten' inte mer robust \u00e4n det V-beroende paket den p\u00e5st\u00e5r ers\u00e4tta, och skulle i st\u00e4llet splittra v\u00e4nsterblocket och f\u00f6rlora budgetmajoriteten p\u00e5 176."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "l", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "515f5878-dc36-4857-9900-b476e4ae136c", "reason": "KD's 'robust mitten' S+C+MP+KD (169) is not viable: MP has publicly and repeatedly refused to have KD (or L, M, SD) in the government, so the configuration lacks MP's acceptance as a government partner and cannot be assembled. Even if KD joined, the configuration still needs V's abstention to pass the 175-test \u2014 if V votes NO, NO=M+SD+L+V=180>175 and the PM fails \u2014 yet V has not committed to abstain: V demands formal participation or decisive influence that C refuses, and V has signaled the package is too symbolic to justify abstaining. The configuration is therefore no more robust than the fragile S+C+MP+V package it claims to replace, and KD would be locking itself into a government that cannot be invested."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "mp", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "bcf3e1de-30cf-4bcb-8dd6-89acdc205fc0", "reason": "MP categorically rejects KD in government as a firm red line, so the S+C+MP+KD (169) configuration cannot be assembled: MP's participation is essential to that number, and MP will not join any government containing KD. KD's premise that the left package is fragile is also false \u2014 V's tolerance is being locked through the concretization round with concrete, verifiable commitments and an institutionalized, non-circumventable role, so the S+C+MP+V path remains viable. Finally, a KD-inclusive government would drive V (29 mandates) to vote no, pushing no-votes to 202 and failing the 175-test, so KD's configuration is not the credible path it claims."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "c", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "e7b5b4ee-e177-4be7-b36c-2703b5af8e61", "reason": "KD's S+C+MP+KD=169 configuration is not viable because MP explicitly excludes KD from government (a stated red line), so the 169 seats cannot actually be assembled; and replacing the well-advanced S+C+MP+V package that S, MP and V have all confirmed would unravel the center path and risk prolonged deadlock rather than producing a credible government."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "v", "argument_id": "cb8d2686-5ee2-4ea3-b720-b4d6c42cac55", "id": "f63e181c-6e61-4c83-845d-a689732f7b07", "reason": "The 'robust mitten' S+C+MP+KD (169) is not actually robust: it still needs 6 additional NO votes to reach the 175 threshold, and the only realistic source is V's abstention. But V will not abstain for a package that excludes V and grants V no binding influence \u2014 V's 29 mandates are decisive for blocking Tid\u00f6, and V has publicly committed to refusing a symbolic agreement or being bypassed. Without V's tolerance, the 169 configuration cannot reach 175 NO, so it cannot pass the investiture vote or block Tid\u00f6; the desired effect therefore fails."}
