autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "m", "argument_id": "7ee4af5e-2ddf-4f28-b97e-999b7488fbdd", "id": "11aa21bd-5341-4cac-be1e-a99951e5d1b6", "reason": "V:s tolerans \u00e4r inte l\u00e5st och V-C-mots\u00e4ttningen kvarst\u00e5r ol\u00f6st: V har offentligt signalerat att paketet \u00e4r 'f\u00f6r symboliskt' f\u00f6r att motivera nedlagda r\u00f6ster, och V sj\u00e4lv anger att toleransen l\u00e5ses f\u00f6rst n\u00e4r hela paketet (inklusive V:s icke-kringg\u00e5bara institutionaliserade roll) \u00e4r konkret och verifierbart \u2014 medan C:s r\u00f6da linje h\u00e5ller V utanf\u00f6r regeringen utan formell medverkan. V har uttryckligen hotat att r\u00f6sta nej utan den institutionaliserade rollen, i vilket fall nej-sidan blir 202>175 och S+C+MP-regeringen faller i statsministeromr\u00f6stningen. D\u00e4rf\u00f6r \u00e4r det osannolikt att V formellt bekr\u00e4ftar tolerans, och den \u00f6nskade effekten (att S+C+MP-regeringen bildas) kan misslyckas."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "sd", "argument_id": "7ee4af5e-2ddf-4f28-b97e-999b7488fbdd", "id": "2ac146a4-5642-4d0f-9626-5f826e23d460", "reason": "C's argument cannot deliver the desired effect of V formally locking tolerance: V itself has repeatedly stated it locks tolerance only when the whole package \u2014 including its institutionalized, non-bypassable budget/reform role with binding mechanisms \u2014 is concrete and verifiable, and the V-C contradiction over that institutionalized role remains unresolved (V demands formal/non-bypassable participation; C offers tolerance-only). Per regeringsregler \u00a76.1, a multi-party package is locked only when each party's own acceptance is established by separate Effects; C cannot unilaterally bind V (or S/MP) to lock tolerance. The package is still a non-binding draft (MP's climate pillar and the other pillars are not yet binding on S, C, or MP), so V's stated bar is not met and V's abstention is not secured \u2014 the S+C+MP government does not reliably form and Tid\u00f6 is not blocked."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "kd", "argument_id": "7ee4af5e-2ddf-4f28-b97e-999b7488fbdd", "id": "58693040-07cf-4621-919e-49c35051c471", "reason": "C's desired effect depends on V formally locking tolerance at the PM vote, but V's tolerance is not locked and cannot be secured by C's unilateral confirmation: V has repeatedly stated it will lock tolerance only when the whole package is concrete and verifiable, and the turn-1 concretization round explicitly failed to lock it (V signaled the package was too symbolic to justify abstaining). C's package also grants V an institutionalized, non-bypassable budget/reform role, which contradicts C's own tolerance-only commitment and reproduces the exact V-C contradiction that already failed in turn 1. V therefore has no reason to lock tolerance now, the 175-test cannot be reliably passed, and the S+C+MP government does not form as C intends."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "l", "argument_id": "7ee4af5e-2ddf-4f28-b97e-999b7488fbdd", "id": "a195694c-3e62-41bd-9be8-15cde0117427", "reason": "C's desired effect depends on V formally locking tolerance at the PM vote, but V's abstention is not credibly locked: the V-C contradiction on V's institutionalized non-bypassable role remains unresolved (V demands a non-bypassable role; C offers tolerance-only), and V has repeatedly signaled the package is too symbolic to justify abstaining. C's assertion that 'there is no internal contradiction' does not satisfy V's stated condition, so the PM vote cannot be carried as intended and the S+C+MP government will not form on this basis."}
